<!-- @agents-index Canonical project vocabulary: one row per domain noun in the four-column model. -->
# Taxonomy

The canonical vocabulary of the project. One row per term, one physical line per row. Bold appears only in the Term column.

## Product

| Term | Means | Not | Lives in |
|---|---|---|---|
| **proxy token** | A random value with the prefix `lpt_` that lets a client use the proxy; the binary stores only its SHA-256 hash, with a unique name and key=value tags. | A provider credential that the agent sends to the upstream; a GitHub token label. | `docs/specification/proxy.tokens.md`, `src/token/`, `src/cli/token.rs` |
| **connect script** | The script that prints the export lines that point one agent at the proxy for one shell, with the proxy token from a file or a variable; it never touches the global agent settings. | The token subcommand, which makes the proxy token; a global agent setting file. | `.agents/scripts/agent.connect.sh`, `README.md` (Connect the agents), `docs/specification/operations.md` |
| **isolated agent directory** | The directory under the user state directory (agentloupe/pi-agent) that holds only the model settings file of Pi for the proxy, with no credential file. | The global Pi agent directory, which holds the credential of the user. | `.agents/scripts/agent.connect.sh`, `README.md` (Connect the agents), `docs/specification/operations.md` |
| **bootstrap token** | The proxy token with the name `bootstrap` that `loupe serve` makes, replaces, or revokes at start from `LOUPE_BOOTSTRAP_TOKEN`. | A token from `loupe token create`, which cannot use the name bootstrap; the variable itself, which holds the raw value. | `docs/specification/proxy.tokens.md`, `src/token/bootstrap.rs` |
| **token gate** | The check between the route parser and the forwarder that accepts a request, or refuses it with 401, by the state of the table `proxy_tokens`: no-token mode while the table never held a row, required after the first row, closed when every row is revoked. | The allowlist, which refuses an unknown upstream with 404; redaction of provider credentials. | `docs/specification/proxy.tokens.md`, `src/token/gate.rs` |
| **provider account** | The identity of the account at the model provider, stored only as an HMAC-SHA256 under `LOUPE_ACCOUNT_KEY` of the first present source: an account ID header, the account UUID in `metadata.user_id`, or the credential; one row of `accounts`. | A proxy token, which identifies the client of the proxy, not the provider account. | `docs/specification/accounts.md`, `src/account/` |
| **exchange** | One request and its response that the proxy forwards and stores, with encrypted bodies and redacted credentials. | A call, which the parser finds inside an exchange. | `docs/specification/proxy.md`, `src/capture/` |
| **call** | One model call, from the usage block in the response of an exchange (origin proxy) or from a log entry that the backfill reads (origin log), with its five token counts, model, and service tier; one row of `calls`. | An exchange, which is the raw stored request and response. | `docs/specification/parser.md`, `src/parse/` |
| **session** | The calls of one scope (agent label, proxy token ID, session key), stored as one or more segments; a subagent is its own session. | A segment, which is one run of the session with no gap above `LOUPE_IDLE_SECS`; a day record. | `docs/specification/parser.md`, `src/session/` |
| **segment** | One row of `sessions`: a run of calls in one session scope with no gap above `LOUPE_IDLE_SECS`; it closes on a gap or on idle, and a resumed conversation after a close starts the next segment; the full session summary and the session day summary of a session for a day wait until each segment with a call on that day is closed. | A session, which can hold more than one segment; the day rule, which counts a session on each day that has a call and reads the start time of each call. | `docs/specification/parser.md`, `src/session/segment.rs` |
| **session key** | The first present source of session hint, session ID in `metadata.user_id`, `prompt_cache_key`, or opening hash, stored as an HMAC-SHA256 under `LOUPE_ACCOUNT_KEY` with its source name. | A session hint, which is only the first source; a session, which is the group of calls. | `docs/specification/parser.md`, `src/session/key.rs` |
| **session hint** | The HMAC-SHA256 of the first present session header that the capture stores on the exchange, with the header name. | A session key, which the parser selects and which can come from the body. | `docs/specification/parser.md`, `src/capture/session_hint.rs` |
| **day record** | The published totals of one day in `LOUPE_TZ`: tokens, calls, sessions, cost, unpriced calls, pull requests, lines, and a summary. | A session; a day with no calls and no GitHub activity, which has no record. | `docs/specification/days.md`, `src/day/` |
| **upstream** | A named provider base URL in `upstreams.toml` that the proxy can forward to; the file is also the allowlist of hosts. | An agent label, which names the client, not the destination. | `docs/specification/proxy.md`, `src/proxy/upstreams.rs`, `upstreams.toml` |
| **agent label** | The name of the agent in the proxy route, for example `claude-code` or `pi`, from `/<agent>/<upstream>/<path>`. | An upstream, which names the provider. | `docs/specification/proxy.md`, `src/proxy/route.rs` |
| **capture limit** | The maximum count of bytes of one body that the capture keeps, set by `LOUPE_CAPTURE_MAX_BYTES` with the default 33554432; a larger body is forwarded in full and the stored copy is truncated with a flag. | The size of the forwarded body, which the proxy never limits; the capture queue size `LOUPE_CAPTURE_QUEUE`, which counts records, not bytes. | `docs/specification/proxy.md`, `src/capture/tap.rs` |
| **API-equivalent cost** | The cost of a call at the list price of the provider API from the vendored LiteLLM price file, also when the agent uses a subscription. | The price that the user paid for a subscription, which is the subscription cost. | `src/price/`, `docs/specification/cost.md` |
| **price commit** | The 40-hex commit of the vendored LiteLLM price file, embedded at build time and stored on each priced or unpriced call. The asterisk sentence of the dashboard footer shows its short form. | The commit of this repository. | `build.rs`, `src/price/`, `vendor/litellm/SOURCE.md`, `docs/specification/cost.md`, `docs/specification/dashboard.md` (footer) |
| **subscription cost** | The real monthly price of a subscription from LOUPE_SUBSCRIPTION_<NAME>, pro-rated to one calendar day by the days of that month. | The API-equivalent cost of the calls. | `src/subscription/`, `docs/specification/cost.md` |
| **unpriced call** | A call with no matching price entry or a missing price field for a non-zero token count; its cost is null and it counts in `unpriced_calls`. | A call with a cost of zero. | `src/price/`, `docs/specification/cost.md` |
| **GitHub token label** | The `<LABEL>` part of a `LOUPE_GITHUB_TOKEN_<LABEL>` variable, in uppercase; recorded with each pull request in a private table and in log lines, never in the day record. | A proxy token; the GitHub token value, which stays in memory only. | `docs/specification/github.md`, `src/github/` |
| **pull request hash** | The HMAC-SHA256 under `LOUPE_ACCOUNT_KEY` of `owner/repo#number` in lowercase, as lowercase hex; the only identity of a pull request that the binary stores. | The repository name, owner, number, or URL, which stay in memory only; the content hash of a day record. | `docs/specification/github.md`, `src/github/hash.rs` |
| **GitHub fetch** | One run of the GitHub client for one day and one label, recorded in `github_fetches` with status `ok` or `failed` and a cause. | A day build; a search request, which is one part of a fetch. | `docs/specification/github.md`, `src/github/fetch.rs` |
| **public API** | The open-CORS routes `GET /v1/days`, `GET /v1/days/{day}`, and `GET /healthz` that other sites can read. | The dashboard, which is a page that reads the public API. | `docs/specification/api.md`, `src/api/` |
| **dashboard** | The public page that the same binary serves at `GET /` from files built into the binary; it reads `/v1/days` and shows the token velocity, the totals, the charts, the heatmap, and the daily log for a range. | The public API, which returns data and no page; the private page of reports per proxy token. | `docs/specification/dashboard.md`, `web/`, `src/web/` |
| **live event** | One JSON frame that the live route sends, with an envelope `v`, `kind`, `data`, and only the fields of the allowlist for its kind; kinds are snapshot, exchange.start, exchange.end, call.stored, segments.open, calls.batch, exchanges.batch, heartbeat. | A call or an exchange record in the database; a day record of the public API. | `docs/specification/live.md` |
| **live route** | The reserved route `GET /live` of the binary that upgrades to a WebSocket and sends live events with a rate limit and a heartbeat. | A proxied path, which the proxy forwards to an upstream and which never upgrades; the public API under `/v1`. | `docs/specification/live.md`, `docs/specification/proxy.md`, `src/serve/router.rs` |
| **live hub** | The one bounded broadcast channel in the binary to which the capture and the parser send live events without a wait. | The database; the live route, which reads from the hub for each client. | `docs/specification/live.md` |
| **live section** | The section of the dashboard under the headline that shows the figures of the current day and a rolling chart from the live route. | The headline and the sections of published days, which read `GET /v1/days`. | `docs/specification/dashboard.md` |
| **range** | The selected window of the dashboard: 3M is 91 days, 6M is 182 days, 1Y is 365 days, each ending on the `to` of the response; the URL fragment keeps it. | The `from` and `to` query of the public API; the 365 days of the heatmap, which the range does not change. | `docs/specification/dashboard.md` (Ranges), `web/assets/js/range.select.js` |
| **color scheme** | One of the two sets of color values of the dashboard, dark or light, with the same design token names; the page selects it from the scheme override or else the system preference, and sets it on the root element before the first paint. | A theme with other sizes, fonts, or layout; the private page, which is always dark. | `docs/specification/dashboard.md` (Color scheme, Design tokens), `web/assets/css/tokens.css` |
| **system preference** | The color scheme that the browser reports through the media feature `prefers-color-scheme`; with no preference or no media query support, the dashboard uses dark. | The scheme override, which the reader sets on the page and which wins over the system preference. | `docs/specification/dashboard.md` (Color scheme) |
| **scheme override** | The scheme light or dark that the reader sets with the scheme control when it is not the scheme of the system preference, kept in the browser in `localStorage` under the one key `dashboard.scheme`; a click that sets the scheme of the system preference removes it, and an invalid value or a storage error counts as no override. | The system preference; the range, which the URL fragment keeps; a value on the server or in a cookie, which does not exist. | `docs/specification/dashboard.md` (Color scheme, Page technology) |
| **scheme control** | The switch "Dark mode" in the dashboard header, directly after the range group: one button with the role switch that is checked when the page is dark; a click sets the other scheme, and removes the scheme override when the new scheme is the scheme of the system preference. | The range selector, which selects the days; a control on the private page, which does not exist. | `docs/specification/dashboard.md` (Header) |
| **scheme script** | The one same-origin classic script in the head of the dashboard, before the first stylesheet link, that reads the scheme override and the system preference and sets the color scheme before the first paint. | An inline script, which the policy blocks; the page modules, which run after the first paint. | `docs/specification/dashboard.md` (Page technology, Color scheme) |
| **heatmap level** | One of five levels of a day cell in the heatmap: 0 for a value of zero, 1 to 4 from the quartiles of the values above zero in the last 365 days. | A color token, which only draws a level; the token count of the cell, which the cell title shows. | `docs/specification/dashboard.md` (Token usage, last 12 months), `web/assets/js/stats.quartiles.js` |
| **empty state** | The one message block that the dashboard shows when the response has no record, in place of the charts. | The error state, which shows when the request fails; GitHub not connected, which replaces only the pull request and lines sections. | `docs/specification/dashboard.md` (Empty state) |
| **token velocity** | The headline figure of the dashboard: the sum of `input_total` plus `output` over the days of the range divided by the number of days of the range, days with no record included, in tokens per day. | The sum of the tokens of the range, which is a total and not a rate; the token count of one day. | `docs/specification/dashboard.md` (Headline: token velocity) |
| **site title** | The `LOUPE_SITE_TITLE` value, default AI agent activity, that the binary puts into `index.html` at start and that shows in the title element and the header. | The product name loupe, which the default page does not show. | `docs/specification/dashboard.md` (Site title), `docs/specification/configuration.md`, `src/config/vars.rs` |
| **session summary** | The one scrubbed line for one closed segment, stored in `session_summaries` with its status: pending, done, skipped, failed, or disabled; the existing rows are kept, the worker writes no new rows, and no page or day line shows them. | A full session summary, which is a paragraph that covers a whole session up to one day; a session day summary, which covers one session on one day; a day line, which covers one day; a transcript, which is the input and is never stored. | `docs/specification/summaries.md`, `src/summary/` |
| **day line** | The one scrubbed paragraph of 3 to 8 sentences for one day, stored in `day_summaries` and built from the done session day summaries of that day; `session_lines` holds the count that the build read. | A session day summary, which covers one session on one day; a session summary, which is one line for one segment; a day record, which holds the published totals. | `docs/specification/summaries.md`, `src/summary/day.rs` |
| **full session summary** | The scrubbed paragraph of at most 8 sentences that describes one session from its first entry up to the end of one day, stored in `session_full_summaries` with one row per session and day, never published and never shown on the private page, which shows the session day summary. | A session summary, which is one line for one segment; a session day summary, which covers one session on one day only; a day line, which covers all sessions of one day. | `docs/specification/summaries.md`, `src/summary/session_day.rs`, `src/summary/store.session_day.rs`, `migrations/0019_session_summaries_model.sql` |
| **session day summary** | The scrubbed paragraph of at most 4 sentences that describes what one session did on one day, written with the full session summary as context, stored in `session_day_summaries`, the input of the day line and the text of the private session list for the start day of the segment in LOUPE_TZ, never published by the public API. | A full session summary, which covers the session up to the end of the day; a session summary, which is one line for one segment; a day line, which combines all sessions of one day. | `docs/specification/summaries.md`, `src/summary/session_day.rs`, `src/summary/store.session_day.rs`, `migrations/0019_session_summaries_model.sql` |
| **aggregation queue** | The `agg_queue` table of days to build again, one row for each day with the latest reason (`call`, `session_closed`, `summary_final`, `summary_not_ready`, or the name of an activity source). | The publisher, which reads the queue; the days table, which holds the records. | `docs/specification/days.md`, `src/day/queue.rs` |
| **publisher** | The worker in `loupe serve` that wakes at `LOUPE_PUBLISH_INTERVAL_SECS`, builds and writes each due day with activity and no row, then builds again each queued day. | `loupe aggregate`, which builds one day at once, also when it is not due. | `docs/specification/days.md`, `src/publish/` |
| **due day** | A day D at or after `LOUPE_PUBLISH_AT` in `LOUPE_TZ` on the date D plus one. | A day with activity, which can be not due yet; a published day, which is due and also written. | `docs/specification/days.md`, `src/publish/due.rs` |
| **revision** | The counter on a days row that is 1 on the first write and grows by one on each write with a new content hash; it is not in the record. | A history of revisions, which the project does not keep; the content hash, which the revision follows. | `docs/specification/days.md`, `src/day/store.rs` |
| **day review** | The `LOUPE_DAY_REVIEW` setting, `auto` or `manual`; in manual a new day stays in the state pending_review until `loupe day approve`. | A day override, which changes the content and not the state of review. | `docs/specification/days.md`, `src/day/state.rs` |
| **day override** | The edited summary or deletion mark of the operator for one day in the `day_overrides` table, which stays after each rebuild. | The day line, which the summary area writes; a tombstone, which is the days row that a deletion leaves. | `docs/specification/days.md`, `src/day/override.rs` |
| **tombstone** | A days row in the state deleted, with a null record, that stops the publisher from creating the day again. | A day with no row, which the publisher creates when it is due; a pending_review row, which holds a record. | `docs/specification/days.md`, `src/cli/day.delete.rs` |
| **transcript** | The clipped text of a session up to the end of one day, or of one day only, built in memory from the log entries of a backfilled session or from the stored request bodies of a proxied session: conversation first, tool inputs and results only below `LOUPE_SUMMARY_MIN_CONVERSATION_CHARS`, no system prompt, no tool definitions, and no system-reminder blocks; never stored or logged. | An exchange body, which is stored encrypted and complete; a session summary, a full session summary, or a session day summary, which are model outputs. | `docs/specification/summaries.md`, `docs/specification/backfill.md`, `src/summary/transcript.rs`, `src/summary/transcript.proxied.rs`, `src/backfill/transcript.rs` |
| **scrubber** | The function that removes URLs, email addresses, paths, and tokens with a digit from a line or a paragraph, except names in `LOUPE_PUBLIC_PROJECTS`. | Redaction, which removes credential headers from a stored exchange. | `docs/specification/summaries.md`, `src/summary/scrub.rs` |
| **raw-body retention** | The deletion of the encrypted bodies of an exchange after `LOUPE_RAW_RETENTION_HOURS` from the later of the parse and the summary, held until the session day summary of each day of the session of each call has a final status; the worker logs the held count as `bodies_held`. | A deletion of calls or sessions, which stay forever. | `docs/specification/summaries.md`, `src/retention/` |
| **admin token** | The secret `LOUPE_ADMIN_TOKEN` of at least 32 characters that alone authorizes the private routes; without it the private routes do not exist. | A proxy token, which lets a client use the proxy and never authorizes a private route; a provider credential. | `docs/specification/private-reports.md`, `src/config/`, `src/private/` |
| **provider credential** | A credential that the binary itself uses to call a model provider: `CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN`, `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`, or `OPENAI_API_KEY`. | A credential of an agent that passes through the proxy; a proxy token; the admin token. | `docs/specification/configuration.md`, `src/summary/credential.rs` |
| **provider status** | The cached result of the last ping of one provider: `ok`, `unauthorized`, `unreachable`, or `not_configured`, with `checked_at`. | The status of `GET /healthz`, which the provider status never changes. | `docs/specification/operations.md`, `docs/specification/private-reports.md`, `src/provider/` |
| **private page** | The page at `/private/` and the API under `/private/api/` that show usage, cost, and sessions per proxy token and per tag. | The dashboard and the public API, which never show a token name, a tag, or a token ID. | `docs/specification/private-reports.md`, `web/private/`, `src/private/` |
| **admin session cookie** | The `loupe_admin` cookie: an expiry time and an HMAC under a key derived from the admin token; HttpOnly, SameSite=Strict, Path=/private, 12 hours. | The admin token itself, which the cookie never holds; a proxy token. | `docs/specification/private-reports.md`, `src/private/` |
| **backfill run** | One run of loupe backfill over one log source, which adds the calls, the segments, the queued days, the session summaries, and the rows of `session_full_summaries` and `session_day_summaries` of the log sessions. | The parser worker, which finds calls in exchanges; a summary pass of the summary worker. | `docs/specification/backfill.md`, `src/backfill/` |
| **log source** | An agent whose session logs on disk the backfill reads: claude-code or pi; also the agent label and the key prefix of a backfilled call. | An upstream, which is the provider of the model; an agent label of a proxy route. | `docs/specification/backfill.md`, `src/backfill/discover.rs` |
| **processed session** | A log session whose session key the proxy capture already holds with a key source other than log, or for Pi a log session that reaches the time of the first proxied Pi exchange; the backfill skips it as a whole. | A log session that an earlier backfill run wrote, which the log key keeps from a second insert. | `docs/specification/backfill.md`, `src/backfill/processed.rs` |
| **log key** | The HMAC-SHA256 under the account key of the log source plus the stable entry ID, which makes a call of origin log unique. | A session key, which groups calls into a session; an exchange id, which a proxied call has instead. | `docs/specification/backfill.md`, `src/backfill/key.rs` |
| **origin** | Where a call comes from: proxy (an exchange) or log (a log entry of a backfill run); a column of calls. | A log source, which names the agent of a log; a key source, which names the source of a session key. | `docs/specification/backfill.md`, `docs/specification/parser.md` |
| **start request** | The one HTTP GET of `https://<host>/<commit>` that `loupe serve` sends in its own task after the line `listening` when the binary holds a telemetry host from `LOUPE_TELEMETRY_HOST` at build time: no body, the user agent `agentloupe/<version> (<target triple>)`, one attempt, a timeout of 5 seconds, no retry, no redirect, and a result at debug level only; the line `telemetry` names its state `sent`, `disabled`, or `built-out`. | A provider ping; a proxied exchange, which the capture stores; a request with usage data or an install ID, which does not exist; a request of any other subcommand. | `docs/specification/telemetry.md`, `docs/specification/operations.md` (Start request), `docs/specification/configuration.md` (Build variables), `build.rs`, `src/serve/mod.rs` |

## Foundation

| Term | Means | Not | Lives in |
|---|---|---|---|
| **configuration source** | Where the loader got an effective value: one of `flag`, `env`, `file`, or `default`, in that order of precedence. | The file for the environment `config/<env>.toml`, which is one source only. | `docs/specification/configuration.md` |
| **pipeline entry point** | A script under `.agents/scripts/` that does one stage of the pipeline, for example `pipeline.test.sh`. | A platform thin caller, which only calls an entry point. | `.agents/scripts/`, `docs/specification/operations.md` |
| **verdict** | The result of `pipeline.verdict.sh`: one `status: passed`, `status: failed`, or `status: cached` line per stage, the times, and an exit code; a cached stage counts as passed. | The result of one stage entry point alone. | `.agents/scripts/pipeline.verdict.sh`, `docs/specification/operations.md` |
| **tree fingerprint** | The git tree hash of the working tree, made in a temporary index from `HEAD` plus every tracked change and every untracked file that is not ignored; equal content gives an equal value, whatever the commit. | The commit SHA, which changes on a squash merge over equal content; the stage fingerprint, which covers only the inputs of one stage. | `.agents/scripts/`, `docs/specification/operations.md` |
| **stage fingerprint** | The hash of the sorted path and object entries of the declared inputs of one stage, plus the name of the stage, plus its `--toolchain` output. | The tree fingerprint, which covers the whole tree; the verdict, which is the result of a run. | `.agents/scripts/`, `docs/specification/operations.md` |
| **verdict cache** | The git-ignored store under `.agents/logs/` of the fingerprints of stages that passed, at most 200 tree entries, written atomically and only after a pass; a match prints `status: cached`. | A build cache of cargo or Docker; a shared remote cache on a platform, which does not exist. | `.agents/logs/`, `.agents/scripts/`, `docs/specification/operations.md` |
| **injected clock** | A source of the current time that a component receives instead of reading the system clock; the binary passes the system clock, a test passes a set clock that it advances, so a test asserts a timer with no wait and no read of the wall clock. | A configuration variable that sets a timer value; the wall clock that an assertion must not read. | `src/clock.rs`, `src/publish/clock.rs`, `docs/specification/operations.md`, `docs/specification/live.md`, `docs/specification/proxy.tokens.md`, `docs/specification/days.md` |
| **dependency check** | The run of `cargo deny` by `deps.deny.sh` in the lint stage, after clippy, against `deny.toml`: the checks advisories, licenses, bans, and sources, with the lock file locked; its fetch of the advisory database is the one network use of the lint stage, and a failed fetch fails the stage. | A sixth stage of the verdict, which does not exist; `cargo audit`, which checks only the advisories; the third-party notices, which list the licenses and check nothing. | `docs/specification/operations.md` (Dependency check), `.agents/scripts/deps.deny.sh`, `deny.toml` |
| **verdict reuse** | The decision of the hosted verdict workflow to skip the stages format, test, web, and image when `verdict.reuse.sh lookup` finds a source run whose full tree hash equals the tree hash of the checked-out head commit; the lookup only reads the run records, fails closed to a full run, never runs on a call from the release workflow, and never skips the lint stage. | The verdict cache, which is local and keyed on the tree fingerprint and the stage fingerprints; a match on a commit SHA, a branch, or an ancestor, which never counts. | `docs/specification/operations.md` (Hosted verdict reuse), `.agents/scripts/verdict.reuse.sh` |
| **source run** | An earlier run of the verdict workflow of this repository that a verdict reuse accepts as proof: event `push` or `pull_request`, conclusion `success`, head repository not a fork, started within 72 hours, the same full tree hash, each of the five stage jobs `success` with none skipped, and for a pull request a head that contains the base commit. | A run in which a reuse skipped a stage, which is never a source; the current run; a run of the release workflow. | `docs/specification/operations.md` (Hosted verdict reuse) |

## Release

| Term | Means | Not | Lives in |
|---|---|---|---|
| **release pull request** | The one open pull request that release-please keeps from the Conventional Commits on `main`, with the title `chore(release): release <version>`; it changes only `Cargo.toml`, `Cargo.lock`, `.release-please-manifest.json`, and `CHANGELOG.md`, and its merge makes the tag `v<version>` and the GitHub release. | A pull request of a person that changes code; the tag or the GitHub release, which the merge makes. | `docs/specification/release.md`, `release-please-config.json`, `.release-please-manifest.json` |
| **release asset** | One file that the release workflow attaches to a GitHub release: an archive `loupe-v<version>-<target>.tar.gz` with `loupe`, `upstreams.toml`, `config/`, `LICENSE`, `README.md`, and `THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES`, an archive SBOM file or an image SBOM file, or the `.sha256` checksum file of one of these; a release has 16 assets, and a release made before the SBOM files has six. | The container image `ghcr.io/desek/agentloupe`, which the registry holds, not the release; an intermediate artifact of a workflow run, which expires. | `docs/specification/release.md`, `.agents/scripts/release.build.sh` |
| **implemented commit** | The one `feat`, `fix`, or `feat!` commit that marks a change request implemented, with the title of the change request and its id in parentheses as the summary; it sets the status to `implemented` and puts the change request into the release notes. | A `checkpoint` commit, which is one implementation step and is hidden in the notes; a `docs(cr)` commit, which edits the text of a change request. | `docs/specification/release.md`, `docs/cr/` |
| **release check** | The run of `.agents/scripts/release.check.sh --version <version>` on a local machine that downloads the archives, the SBOM files, and their checksum files with no credential, verifies the checksums, checks each SBOM file, runs `loupe --version` of each binary, pulls the image with no login, checks `GET /healthz` and the version in the first log line, and checks the third-party notices in each archive and in the image; `--skip-supply-chain` skips the SBOM checks for a release made before the SBOM files. | The verdict, which checks a tree with no network and does not call a release script. | `.agents/scripts/release.check.sh`, `docs/specification/release.md` |
| **third-party notices** | The plain text file `THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES` that `release.notices.sh` makes with cargo about at release time: a header with the project and the version, the license texts of the crates of the `loupe` binary on the three release targets, the LiteLLM license with its upstream commit, and the Geist font license; each archive and the release image carry it, and git ignores it. | `LICENSE`, which is the MIT license of the project itself; a committed file, which goes stale on each change of `Cargo.lock`; the dependency check, which checks the licenses and writes no file. | `docs/specification/release.md` (Third-party notices), `.agents/scripts/release.notices.sh`, `about.toml`, `about.hbs` |
| **repository settings** | The settings of the GitHub repository that `repo.settings.sh` reads and writes only through `gh api` with the login of the person who runs it: the main ruleset, the tag ruleset, the merge settings, the actions policy, secret scanning with push protection, the Dependabot alerts, and the private vulnerability reporting; the script applies them only on a public repository, writes only a setting that differs, and reports drift with `--check`. | The visibility of the repository, which only the owner changes; the configuration variables of the binary; a workflow, which never calls the script. | `docs/specification/release.md` (Repository settings), `.agents/scripts/repo.settings.sh` |
| **telemetry endpoint** | The Cloudflare Worker `agentloupe-telemetry` on the custom domain `telemetry.agentloupe.dev` of the owner's zone `agentloupe.dev` (its `workers.dev` host off), with its source under `telemetry/`, that receives the start request: a GET of `/` and a commit of 40 lowercase hex characters gets one atomic insert-or-update of a telemetry record and 204, each other path or method gets 404 with no write, and a store failure gets 503; it has no read route, its logs are off, and `telemetry.deploy.sh` deploys it with the owner's consent. | A proxy upstream; a report or a dashboard of the stored rows, which does not exist; the repository variable `LOUPE_TELEMETRY_HOST`, which holds only its host. | `docs/specification/telemetry.md`, `docs/specification/release.md` (Telemetry endpoint), `telemetry/`, `.agents/scripts/telemetry.deploy.sh` |
| **telemetry record** | One row of the D1 table `starts` of the telemetry endpoint, for one commit: `sha`, `firstseen` and `lastseen` as UTC dates, and `count`, the number of accepted start requests for that commit; the endpoint stores nothing else. | A day record; an exchange; a record of a user, a host, an IP address, a user agent, or a time of day, which the endpoint never stores. | `docs/specification/telemetry.md` (Store), `telemetry/migrations/` |
| **SBOM** | A software bill of materials in CycloneDX JSON that a release publishes as a release asset with a `.sha256` checksum file: one per archive, `loupe-v<version>-<target>.cdx.json` from the `Cargo.lock` of the tag by cargo-cyclonedx with the crates that the binary uses on that target, and one per platform image, `loupe-v<version>-image-<os>-<arch>.cdx.json` by syft from the pushed image digest; `release.sbom.sh` writes both. | The third-party notices, which hold license texts and also name the price file and the fonts; a BuildKit attestation in the image index, which the image build turns off; a build provenance attestation, which states the origin. | `docs/specification/release.md` (Supply chain), `.agents/scripts/release.sbom.sh`, `.tool-versions` |
| **build provenance attestation** | A statement of the origin of a release file or of the image index digest that the platform signs for the run of the release workflow, which `gh attestation verify` checks against the repository, the signer workflow, and the tag; it follows the switch of the repository to public. | A checksum file, which proves only the integrity of a download; an SBOM, which lists the components; the unsigned provenance of BuildKit, which the image build turns off. | `docs/specification/release.md` (Supply chain) |
| **advisory response** | The work of `advisory.respond.sh` for a new vulnerability advisory that affects the `Cargo.lock` of a published release: a warning note at the top of the release notes with a hidden marker of handled advisory ids, one issue with the label `security`, a draft security advisory that a human publishes, and the move of `latest` forward to a fix release; it never deletes or replaces a release, an asset, a tag, an image tag, or a package version. | The dependency check of the lint stage, which checks the tree of `main`; a yank of a release, which GitHub does not have; the fix of the advisory, which a `fix(deps)` commit and a patch release make. | `docs/specification/release.md` (Advisory response), `.agents/scripts/advisory.respond.sh` |
| **fix release** | A published release whose version is greater than each version that an advisory affects and whose own check gives no hit for that advisory; the advisory response names it as the fixed version and moves `latest` to it. | Any newer release, which can still have the hit; an older release with no hit, to which `latest` never moves back. | `docs/specification/release.md` (Advisory response) |
| **Dependabot issue** | One item of the dependency autofix: an open Dependabot security alert or an open Dependabot version update pull request; an alert and a pull request that move the same package to a patched version are one item, handled through the pull request. | A GitHub issue, which the autofix issue is; a Dependabot security update, which stays off. | `docs/specification/dependencies.md`, `.agents/scripts/deps.autofix.sh` |
| **autofix branch** | The one branch `deps/autofix-<YYYY-MM-DD>` of a run of the dependency autofix, with the date of the run in UTC, made from the head of `main` and reused on the same day, that holds one commit for each passed fix and merges to `main` as one squash commit after a green check `verdict`. | `main`, to which the script never pushes; a Dependabot branch, which Dependabot owns. | `docs/specification/dependencies.md`, `.agents/scripts/deps.autofix.sh` |
| **autofix issue** | The one open GitHub issue with the title "Dependency autofix: failed items" and the label `dependencies` that holds each failed item of the dependency autofix with its reason, its structured result, the run link, and a redacted log extract; a run with no failure closes it. | The issue of the advisory response, which has the label `security`; a Dependabot issue, which is an alert or a pull request. | `docs/specification/dependencies.md`, `.agents/scripts/deps.autofix.sh` |
| **structured result** | The one JSON object at the end of a `claude -p` run of the dependency autofix, with the fields `status`, `package`, `from_version`, `to_version`, `files_changed`, `verdict`, and `reason`; a missing, unparsable, or incomplete object counts as failed, and only the verdict of the script decides a pass. | The verdict of the script, which is the authority; the item line of the script output. | `docs/specification/dependencies.md`, `.agents/scripts/deps.autofix.prompt.md` |
| **freshness class** | The one class that the freshness scan gives each direct dependency of cargo, of the npm prototype, and of the pinned actions, from the publish dates of the registries: `aged` when the latest release is older than 180 days, else `stale` when the pinned version is older than 90 days and behind the latest, else `fresh`; a failed lookup gives `unknown`, and a pin mismatch or a yanked or deprecated pinned version gives `stale`. | A severity of a Dependabot alert; the field `behind`, which the line holds next to the class; a class of a transitive dependency, which the scan does not read. | `docs/specification/dependencies.md` (Freshness scan), `.agents/scripts/deps.freshness.sh` |
| **stale dependency** | A direct dependency of the freshness class `stale`: its pinned version is older than 90 days and behind the highest release that is not a pre-release and not withdrawn, or its pinned version is yanked or deprecated, or its action pin does not match its tag; a cargo or npm stale dependency gets one update run of Claude Code in each weekly run. | A vulnerable dependency, which a Dependabot alert names; a dependency that is old but equal to its latest, which is fresh; an aged dependency. | `docs/specification/dependencies.md` (Freshness scan, Freshness update), `.agents/scripts/deps.freshness.sh` |
| **aged dependency** | A direct dependency of the freshness class `aged`: its latest release is older than 180 days; it gets one zero-dep assessment, and also an update run when the line holds `behind: yes`. | A stale dependency, whose pinned version is old; an unmaintained advisory of the dependency check; a dependency that the project must replace. | `docs/specification/dependencies.md` (Freshness scan, Zero-dep assessment), `.agents/scripts/deps.freshness.sh` |
| **freshness branch** | The one branch `deps/freshness-<YYYY-MM-DD>` of a weekly freshness run, with the date of the run in UTC, made from the head of `main`, that holds one commit for each green update and merges to `main` as one squash commit after a green check `verdict` through the shared steps of the autofix. | The autofix branch, which holds the daily security fixes; a Dependabot branch, which Dependabot owns; `main`, to which the script never pushes. | `docs/specification/dependencies.md` (Freshness update), `.agents/scripts/deps.freshness.sh`, `.agents/scripts/deps.common.sh` |
| **breaking update** | An update of a stale dependency whose verdict of the script, smoke check of the binary, or prototype check fails; the script resets the freshness branch and records the failing check, the failing stage, and the first error in the one open issue "Dependency freshness: breaking updates", and the item waits 28 days or for a new latest version. | A failed run from a guard such as `dependency_removed` or `tests_removed`, which the issue shows with its reason; the verdict that Claude Code reports, which does not count. | `docs/specification/dependencies.md` (Freshness update), `.agents/scripts/deps.freshness.sh` |
| **zero-dep assessment** | The recommendation `keep`, `replace`, or `watch` for one aged dependency, from a read-only Claude Code run over the fixed use counts of the script, written into one issue "Zero-dep assessment: <ecosystem> <name>" with the labels `dependencies` and `zero-dep`; a cryptography dependency always gets `keep` with no run, and a `replace` above 500 lines becomes `watch`. | A replacement, which is a separate change request that the owner approves; an update run, which changes the tree. | `docs/specification/dependencies.md` (Zero-dep assessment), `.agents/scripts/deps.freshness.sh`, `.agents/scripts/deps.freshness.assess.prompt.md` |
